  "id": "COMPOUND:31451 - PROTEIN:4961",
  "verbalization": "Propenyl propyl disulfide is implicated in the biological activity of FaDu through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for multiple metabolites, including (5R,8R,9R,10R,13R,14R,17S)-17-[(2R)-5-(2-hydroxypropan-2-yl)-2-methyloxolan-2-yl]-4,4,8,10,14-pentamethyl-1,2,5,6,7,9,11,12,13,15,16,17-dodecahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-one, 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, and 5-Hydroxytryptophan monohydrate, dl-. These metabolites are all known to interact with FaDu, indicating a potential pathway where Propenyl propyl disulfide serves as a common target. The integration of these findings suggests that Propenyl propyl disulfide may exert its biological effects through a shared mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of these metabolites, which in turn influence FaDu. The evidence supports a role for Propenyl propyl disulfide in the regulation of FaDu, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
